  "body": "## What changed\n\nFollow-up to #132 (merged before this commit was pushed). Adds `scripts/gate.sh`, a bash 3.2 port of `scripts/gate.ps1`, so macOS and Linux contributors can run the gates without installing PowerShell:\n\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick [base]`, `batch`, `release`, `test <name> [crate] [--exact] [--ignored]`\n- same cargo invocations, per-step logs under `gate-logs/`, same summary.\n- quick tier: runs every suite of each touched crate (not only changed `#[test]` fns) - slower, never narrower; shared crates / Cargo changes widen to batch, as in gate.ps1.\n- `.gitattributes`: `*.sh text eol=lf`, so the script stays runnable from a Windows checkout; file mode 755.\n- README names both scripts.\n\n## Testing\n\n`bash -n` clean; dry runs of batch, quick and test modes print the expected cargo commands. Not run end-to-end on a Mac - asked the #129 reporter to try it.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #129\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
